claimed: okay-script-persistent-sessions -- the second okay-script-site follow-on (filed 2026-09-06): Sessions backed by okay-persist so a Site's sessions survive a restart. okay.script.Sessions becomes a trait (handle(existing, now): Handle; size) with two implementations: Sessions.memory(ttl) (today's ConcurrentHashMap, still the default) and Sessions.persisted(store: okay.persist.Store, ttl, topic) -- one key per session, the full attribute map + last-access time as the value (Snapshots-style keep-latest, tombstone on invalidate), an in-memory index rebuilt by scanning the log on open, Ack.Durable per write. Touches build.sbt (okayScript gains okayPersist.jvm as a MAIN dependency), Site.scala, specs/okay-script.md; tests on MemoryStore and a FileStore reopened from disk.
